kiremote Debian packaging
=========================

Four binary packages from one build of the top-level Makefile:

    kiremote            kiremoted and kiremote-cli (+ translations, autostart)
    kiremote-gtk        the GTK2 window and tray icon, for any desktop;
                        depends on kiremote (= same version)
    kiremote-kidesktop  the kiconf tab, the xisserve page and the xispanel
                        widget; depends on kiremote (= same version) and
                        kidesktop-core (>= 0.1.4~)

    kiremote-mirror     the phone's screen in a window (libavcodec, libswscale,
                        libpulse) and the scrcpy-server it copies to the
                        phone; depends on kiremote (= same version), which
                        holds the translations. The interfaces only Suggest
                        it: it brings ffmpeg's libraries.

Each package's directory is filled by `make install-daemon`, `install-gtk`,
`install-kidesktop` and `install-mirror`. The last one downloads the
scrcpy-server jar from scrcpy's release and checks it against the SHA-256 in
config.mk (scripts/fetch-scrcpy-server.sh), so building the package needs
network access and curl.

kidesktop-core is a Build-Depends only for the headers the widget and the
page are compiled against (xispanel_widget.h, xisserve_page.h); the version
has a "~" because its own per-distro builds are 0.1.4~ubuntu22.04, which is
older than a bare 0.1.4. The modules are checked at run time by the ABI
numbers in those headers (both 1 today): when kidesktop bumps one, the
Depends here must follow.

debian/changelog is not kept in git: scripts/build-deb.sh writes it for each
build, with the version from the git tag (v1.2.3 -> 1.2.3, or
<VERSION in config.mk>+git<date>.<commit> between tags) plus a distro suffix
(~ubuntu22.04, ~debian12), as kidesktop does.

    ./scripts/install-build-deps.sh   # apt Build-Depends (+ kidesktop-core, see the script)
    ./scripts/build-deb.sh            # -> dist/*.deb
